# Cursor UI Component Patterns — COYOTE BURGUER

When generating or editing UI components, apply these exact code patterns instead of generic Shadcn/Tailwind defaults.

## 1. JSX / Tailwind Component Blueprints

### Primary CTA Button
```tsx
<button
  className="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-5 py-3 font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-wider transition-transform hover:-translate-x-0.5 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
  style={{
    backgroundColor: "#B13B29",
    color: "#FAF8F5",
    border: "2px solid #B13B29",
    borderRadius: "6px",
    boxShadow: "4px 4px 0px #14110F",
  }}
>
  {children}
</button>
```

### Elevated Feature / Product Card
```tsx
<article
  className="p-6"
  style={{
    backgroundColor: "#262320",
    color: "#C4B5A6",
    border: "2px solid #B13B29",
    borderRadius: "10px",
    boxShadow: "4px 4px 0px #14110F",
  }}
>
  {children}
</article>
```

### Stamp / Pill Badge
```tsx
<span
  className="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 text-xs font-mono font-bold uppercase"
  style={{
    backgroundColor: "#6896D8",
    color: "#141210",
    border: "2px solid #B13B29",
    borderRadius: "9999px",
  }}
>
  {label}
</span>
```

## 2. Hard Anti-Patterns
- Do NOT use glossy corporate SaaS gradients, neon purple/cyan, or glassmorphism
- Do NOT use sterile pure #FFFFFF backgrounds — always use warm sandstone/adobe cream or deep earth charcoal
- Do NOT use generic stock-photo icons; use bold folk-art silhouettes and stamp borders

- Forbidden Color: Generic SaaS indigo/violet (#6366F1, #8B5CF6)
- Forbidden Color: Unrelated neon cyan (#00FFFF) unless explicitly in accent tokens
